## Project Context

This project uses the Techversant AI development workflow:
Analysis → Plan → Arch Design → UX Design → Execution → AI Review → Manual Review → QA → CI/CD → Deploy

Tech stack: {{BACKEND_STACK}} | {{FRONTEND_STACK}} | {{DATABASE}} | {{CLOUD_PROVIDER}}

---

## Core Rules

### Never Do
- Write code without an approved spec or task
- Hardcode secrets, tokens, or credentials
- Use string concatenation in SQL queries
- Skip tenant_id scoping on any database query  ← SaaS/multi-tenant projects only; remove this rule for single-tenant systems
- Leave TODO comments without a ticket reference
- Commit directly to main or dev
- Write ORM queries in hot paths — use direct SQL
- Catch exceptions you can't meaningfully handle
- Add features beyond what the task requires

### Always Do
- Validate input at every API boundary
- Return structured error responses with consistent shape
- Add audit log entries for every state change
- Use parameterized queries for all SQL
- Scope every DB query by tenant_id  ← SaaS/multi-tenant only; omit for single-tenant projects
- Write tests for happy path + at least 2 edge cases
- Follow Conventional Commits: feat/fix/chore/docs/refactor/test
- Check `.claude/rules/` for the relevant standard before implementing

---

## Code Style

### General
- Functions do one thing — if you need "and" to describe it, split it
- Name variables and functions for what they ARE, not what they DO
- Explicit over implicit — no magic, no hidden conventions
- No dead code — delete what isn't used
- Comments only for non-obvious WHY — not WHAT

### Backend ({{BACKEND_STACK}})
- Controllers/handlers are thin — delegate to services
- Services contain business logic — no DB calls directly
- Repositories handle all data access — return domain objects
- Errors propagate up — handle only at boundaries
- All async functions must handle rejection

### Frontend ({{FRONTEND_STACK}})
- Components are dumb — no business logic, no direct API calls
- State lives as high as needed, no higher
- Use design system tokens — no hardcoded colors or spacing
- Every interactive element must be keyboard-accessible
- Mobile-first — test at 390px minimum

### Database ({{DATABASE}})
- Schema changes via migrations only — never alter prod directly
- Every migration must have a rollback
- Indexes on all foreign keys and commonly filtered columns
- No nullable columns without a documented reason

